course: dictionary
lesson: 16114
title: The word wetting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wetting is the -ing form of the verb wet. It means making something wet with water or another liquid. «Wetting your hair before you shampoo it helps the soap spread.» Here wetting is the first job you do, before the soap goes on.
explain: Wetting can also be a noun. In health talk, bedwetting means passing wee by accident while asleep. «Bedwetting is common in younger children, and a doctor can help.» The clues are bed, asleep and wee, so you can work out the meaning from the words around it.
explain: Scientists and artists use wetting too. «We tested three paper towels by wetting each one and counting the drops it soaked up.» Wetting means adding water, so the test shows which towel is most absorbent. Always check the sentence to see what job the word does.
fact: Wetting means making something wet with water or another liquid.
fact: Wetting is the -ing form of the verb wet: wet, wets, wetting.
fact: «Bedwetting» means passing wee by accident while asleep.
fact: Bedwetting is common in younger children and is nothing to be ashamed of; doctors and parents help with it kindly.
fact: In art, wetting paper before watercolour painting helps the paint spread smoothly.
exercise: «Wetting the cloth first helped Mia clean the cut.» What is wetting doing to the cloth? | Putting it away in a drawer | Painting a picture on it | Tearing it into strips | *Making it wet with water
exercise: «Bedwetting is common in younger children.» What does bedwetting mean? | Sleeping in a tent in the garden | Having a bath just before bed | *Passing wee by accident while asleep | Making the bed very neatly
exercise: Before watercolour painting, Ana was wetting her paper. Why might an artist do this? | To turn the paper into card | To make the paper heavier to carry | *To help the paint spread smoothly | To hide the picture from others
test: Which word is the -ing form of the verb wet? | wetted | wets | *wetting | wetter
test: «Wetting your hair before shampoo helps the soap spread.» What does wetting mean in this sentence? | *Making something wet with water | Brushing your hair neatly | Cutting your hair short | Drying your hair with a towel
exam: Which best describes bedwetting? | A kind of bath for dolls | A way to dry the sheets | Wetting the bed on purpose as a joke | *Passing wee by accident while asleep, and nothing to be ashamed of
